LIKEOS-INSTALL(1)            System Administration           LIKEOS-INSTALL(1)

NAME
       likeos-install - install LikeOS on a disk, in a text terminal

SYNOPSIS
       likeos-install [--verbose] [--no-reboot]
       likeos-install --answers file [--yes] [--dry-run] [--no-reboot] [--ver-
       bose]
       likeos-install --list-disks
       likeos-install --reset-tty

DESCRIPTION
       likeos-install installs LikeOS from the medium it was started from onto
       a  disk of the computer: it partitions the disk (or uses a partition of
       it), creates the file systems, unpacks the system image,  sets  up  the
       new  system  --  language, time zone, keyboard, computer name, the root
       password and a user account --, installs the boot  loader  on  the  EFI
       system partition, registers it with the firmware, and restarts the com-
       puter into the installed system.

       It  is the text-mode counterpart of the graphical installer, likeos-in-
       staller(1), and does the same work through the same installer  library;
       the  installation  medium offers it when the graphical installer cannot
       run (a computer whose graphics do not work), and it runs in any  termi-
       nal, also over a serial line or ssh(1).  It must run as root.

   Interactive installation
       Started  without  --answers,  likeos-install  asks the questions of the
       graphical installer, one at a time: the language of the installed  sys-
       tem  and  the  format of dates and times, the disk to install on (to be
       erased completely, or one of its partitions), the time zone,  the  key-
       board layouts (up to four), the computer's name, the root password, and
       the  name,  user name and password of the account to sign in with; then
       it shows a summary and asks for a last confirmation before anything  is
       written  to  the disk.  Typing back (or <) at a question returns to the
       one before; Ctrl-C or the end of the input cancels the installation  --
       until  the  confirmation  nothing  has been changed.  On a terminal the
       progress of the installation is a bar that  redraws  itself;  when  the
       standard  input  or  output  is not a terminal every question reads one
       line and the progress is printed line by line, so the  program  can  be
       driven by another program or logged.

   Unattended installation
       With --answers file the answers are read from file instead (see likeos-
       install.conf(5)),  and nothing is asked but the confirmation before the
       disk is changed, which --yes gives in advance.

   What is installed
       Erasing the whole disk gives it a new GUID  partition  table  with  two
       partitions:  an  EFI  system partition of 512 MiB (FAT32, label LIKEOS-
       ESP) and the LikeOS root file system (ext4, label likeos-root)  in  the
       rest  of  the disk.  Installing on one partition formats that partition
       with ext4 and uses the EFI system partition the disk has already  (FAT,
       at  least  100 MB; the first one when there are several).  LikeOS needs
       at  least  the  size  the  system  image  asks  for   (/install/likeos-
       rootfs.tar.zst.info).

       The system image is /install/likeos-rootfs.tar.zst, checked against its
       checksum (/install/likeos-rootfs.tar.zst.sha256) before it is unpacked.
       The  installed  system  gets  an  /etc/fstab naming its file systems by
       UUID,    the    boot    loader    in    \EFI\LIKEOS\BOOTX64.EFI    (and
       \EFI\BOOT\BOOTX64.EFI  as  the  firmware's  fallback) on its EFI system
       partition, and a firmware boot entry labelled LikeOS first in the  boot
       order (see likeos-efiboot(1)).  It starts straight into LikeOS, without
       the boot menu of the installation medium.

OPTIONS
       --answers file
              Install unattended, with the answers in file.

       --list-disks
              List  the  disks LikeOS can be installed on, and exit.  The disk
              the running system was started from cannot be chosen.

       --dry-run
              Do everything but change the disk: check the answers,  work  out
              and  show  the  plan (partitions, file systems, what is erased),
              then stop.

       --yes  Do not ask for the last confirmation before the disk is changed.
              Meant for --answers; it is the caller's  confirmation  that  the
              disk named there may be erased.

       --no-reboot
              Do  not  restart the computer when the installation is done (the
              reboot setting of an answer file is overridden).

       --verbose
              Show the installer's log lines (each step, each program it  runs
              and its result) as well as the progress.

       --reset-tty
              Put  the terminal on the standard input back into line mode with
              echo (line editing, echo, Ctrl-C and the other signal keys, car-
              riage return read as newline, newline written as carriage return
              and newline), and exit.  An installation  turns  echo  and  line
              mode  off and puts them back when it ends; a likeos-install that
              was killed cannot, and the installation medium's console session
              runs this before each of its menus.  It fails  (exit  status  4)
              when the standard input is not a terminal.

EXIT STATUS
       0      LikeOS  was  installed  (or, with --dry-run or --list-disks, the
              plan or the list was shown; with --reset-tty, the  terminal  was
              reset).

       not 0  The installation failed or was cancelled, or the command line or
              the  answer file had a mistake; the reason is shown, and the log
              says more.

FILES
       /install/likeos-rootfs.tar.zst
              The system image that is installed, with its checksum  (.sha256)
              and a description (.info).

       /tmp/likeos-install.log
              The  log  of  the  installation; a copy is kept on the installed
              system as /var/log/likeos-install.log.

       /mnt/likeos
              Where the new system's file systems are mounted during  the  in-
              stallation.

EXAMPLES
       Install on /dev/nvme0n1 without questions, erasing it:

              cat > answers.conf <<'EOF'
              disk=/dev/nvme0n1
              whole_disk=yes
              locale=de_DE.UTF-8
              timezone=Europe/Berlin
              keyboard=de
              hostname=office-pc
              user_fullname="Erika Mustermann"
              user_name=erika
              user_password_hash=$y$j9T$...
              EOF
              likeos-install --answers answers.conf --dry-run
              likeos-install --answers answers.conf --yes

